  "description": "UQOJUH crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C323 H428 Dy12 N48 O71,3(C4 H8 O2),6(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1'? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors; Dy3'? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors; Dy5'? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors; Dy6'? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.703-3.950 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.41-111.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy12(1-3H)3(1-2H)3(PhCO2)5(OH)16(H2O)21]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 16 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 21 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
